# Design Decisions Log
Format: DECISION | RATIONALE | TRADEOFF

---

## Hardware & Runtime

**[2026-08-26] Run UV-Net on M4 CPU, no GPU**
UV-Net inference on a single part graph (few hundred nodes) takes <1s on CPU. For a POC demo with a pre-indexed library, this is fast enough. Log `graph_ms`, `uvnet_ms`, `faiss_ms` on search responses — "CPU, ~400ms, no GPU" is a strong demo talking point.
Tradeoff: bottleneck at concurrent uploads in production. Fix: batch indexing pipeline + GPU worker.

---

## ML Architecture

**[2026-08-26] UV-Net for CAD embedding, not AAGNet**
UV-Net has a pre-trained model in `cad-feature-detection/feature_detector/model.tar.gz` with the full inference pipeline (occwl + DGL). AAGNet has richer instance segmentation but requires different gAAG preprocessing and has no pre-trained weights readily available in the workspace.
Tradeoff: UV-Net global embeddings don't identify *which* faces make two parts similar — AAGNet would. Acceptable for POC; call this out in the demo as a v2 improvement.

**[2026-08-26] Use UV-Net's `graph_emb` (128-dim), not mean-pooled node features**
UV-Net's `GraphEncoder.forward()` returns `(node_emb, graph_emb)`. `graph_emb` is max-pooled across GNN layers and is what the model was trained to produce — 128-dim, not 512-dim. Mean-pooling last-layer node features throws away the model's own pooling design.
Tradeoff: none. This is the correct usage of the model.

**[2026-08-26] Keep UV-Net segmentation head for feature histograms**
The segmentation head (already in the checkpoint) takes `node_emb` → per-face machining feature labels. Run it at no extra cost during indexing to produce a feature histogram (holes, fillets, pockets, chamfers). Used for chips on result cards, enriching text embeddings, and optional Jaccard overlap score. This is the "feature understanding layer" referenced in `ref.md` without needing AAGNet.
Tradeoff: segmentation head was trained on MFCAD classes; labels on unusual geometry may be noisy. Show chips as indicative, not authoritative.

**[2026-08-26] sentence-transformers MiniLM for text embeddings, Claude/Gemini for explanations only**
Anthropic has no dedicated embeddings endpoint. `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` runs locally (384-dim, CPU-fast). Claude/Gemini called only for the 2–3 sentence "why similar" explanation — keeps API cost near zero for the demo.
Tradeoff: MiniLM quality is lower than OpenAI text-embedding-3-large. Acceptable for metadata strings ("aluminum bracket M6 holes CNC"). Swap in production.

---

## Search Architecture

**[2026-08-26] Two separate FAISS indexes + scalar score fusion (replaced concat + weighted-sum)**
Original design had concat(geo, text) as one vector and weighted-sum in the same sentence — these are mutually exclusive operations. Fixed to: two separate FAISS flat indexes (128-dim geo, 384-dim text), cosine similarity returns scalars, fusion is `0.7 * geo_score + 0.3 * text_score`. Weights are config, not magic numbers.
Tradeoff: two indexes to maintain. At 30–100 parts this is trivial; at scale, replace with a single vector DB that supports named namespaces (Qdrant collections).

**[2026-08-26] Text-only search uses text_index only, not a "slice" of a concat index**
If the index is concatenated geo+text, a text-only query that zeros the geo dims will still pull toward geometry. The text path queries only `text_index`, skipping UV-Net and pythonOCC entirely. CAD-only query uses only `geo_index`.

**[2026-08-26] FAISS flat index (brute force) for POC**
For a 30–100 part demo library, brute force L2 is instant and avoids IVF cluster tuning. Switch to FAISS IVFFlat at ~10k parts.
Tradeoff: does not scale. Fine — we're demoing the concept not the infra.

**[2026-08-26] Geometric fingerprints (OCC stats) as tie-breakers**
When UV-Net scores cluster (e.g. simple prismatic blocks), bbox aspect ratios, volume, and face count break ties and provide explanation fodder ("similar bounding box, similar face count"). Zero extra ML — pythonOCC already has the solid.

---

## LLM / NL

**[2026-08-26] LLM_PROVIDER env var + single adapter function**
`LLM_PROVIDER` = `"anthropic"` | `"gemini"` | `"none"`. One 20-line adapter behind `explain()`. Default `"none"` → template explanation from scores + overlapping feature tags. Demo cannot die on API auth issues.

**[2026-08-26] Cache LLM explanations in SQLite by (query_hash, result_id)**
Repeat demo clicks on the same result do not re-bill the API and respond instantly.

---

## System Architecture

**[2026-08-26] Start fresh (not extending Palmetto)**
Palmetto's C++ engine (OpenCASCADE + Analysis Situs) is tightly coupled to its own pipeline. We only need pythonOCC + occwl for STEP → DGL graph. Starting fresh keeps the codebase clean and every line explainable in an interview.
Tradeoff: rebuild STEP upload + 3D viewer (~1 day). Worth it for clarity.

**[2026-08-26] All search weights and thresholds are config, not hardcoded**
`GEO_WEIGHT`, `TEXT_WEIGHT`, `DUP_THRESHOLD`, `WEAK_THRESHOLD`, `TOP_K` live in `config.py` sourced from env vars. Interview story: "in production, we learn these weights from click data" — the click log table is already in the SQLite schema.

**[2026-08-26] Assembly support deferred**
Multi-body STEP files: embed each body separately, store `parent_id`, query takes max body score. Correct approach but adds a loop and complicates glTF export. For POC, warn the user ("multi-body detected, embedding first solid only") and log. V2.

**[2026-08-26] VLM-CADFeatureRecognition not used**
Image-based approach requires a rendering pipeline (STEP → multi-view images). Adds complexity with no architectural gain over UV-Net for this use case. Could be a complementary v2 search mode ("find parts that look like this image").

**[2026-08-26] AAGNet deferred to v2**
Would add instance segmentation for richer face-level metadata. The segmentation head already on the UV-Net checkpoint gives us 80% of the value (feature histograms) without a second model. AAGNet v2: run at index time to enrich SQLite metadata.

---

## Demo / Testing

**[2026-08-26] `eval_retrieval.py` golden script before any UI work**
8 labeled queries with expected top-3 results and score thresholds. Run before opening Vite. Know that UV-Net actually ranks the near-duplicate first before being on stage.

**[2026-08-26] `demo_metadata.json` written as search documents, not labels**
Tokens should be what an engineer would type: `M6`, `counterbore`, `6061`, `anodize`, `thin wall`. Include `known_issues` and `ppap_notes` even if fake — they power the Costing-prior rail and MiniLM. Include 2–3 parts sharing a supplier so "supplier recommendation" is a live result, not a roadmap slide.

---

## Open Questions / Future Decisions

- Fine-tuning UV-Net on Pre6's actual historical parts (requires labeled internal dataset)
- Production embedding store: Qdrant vs Weaviate vs pgvector
- Auth / multi-tenant: which Pre6 customer's library is searched (data isolation)
- GEO_WEIGHT / TEXT_WEIGHT: learn from click log in production vs. keep heuristic
- Drawings / PPAP PDFs: `pypdf` extract text → MiniLM (no VLM needed for v2 document search)
